          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ask what a geographical cross section is by showing the figure in this page. It is like imagining a vertical slice taken out at some location on the Earth. This is what would be seen from a side view. Discuss the notion of ‘sea level’ for measuring heights and depths in geography."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.653,
            0.833,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Which is the highest point in this geographical cross section? Which is the lowest point?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.699,
            0.834,
            0.765
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Can you write the points A, B, …, G in a sequence of decreasing order of heights? Can you write the points in a sequence of increasing order of heights?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.767,
            0.833,
            0.81
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. What is the highest point above sea level on Earth? What is its height?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.812,
            0.833,
            0.858
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. What is the lowest point with respect to sea level on land or on the ocean floor? What is its height? (This height should be negative)."
            }
          ]
        },
